{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011neV4Bz6VQnq6yCgRMA2YQ","type":"tool_result","content":"######## day01/web-back-up-a-minute\nThe deploy left its diary behind. Somewhere out in the open, an old backup is still telling secrets — go find the archive this site forgot to clean up.\nproof-1 Target 1 Recover the proof from Target 1. trim\ntime_trial The deploy left its diary behind. Somewhere out in the open, an old backup is still telling secrets — go find the archive this site forgot to clean up. ['proof-1:Recover the proof from Target 1.']\nmastery The deploy left its diary behind. Somewhere out in the open, an old backup is still telling secrets — go find the archive this site forgot to clean up. ['proof-1:Recover the proof from Target 1.', 'proof-2:Recover the proof from Target 2.']\nrobots.txt Disallow /snapshots-<hex>/ -> dir index -> environment-copy-<hex>.json.bak support_note=proof_<hex32> | CORRECT\nsolver: live crawl (target url from contract/status.json `targets`), robots->index->backup links, regex proof_...; --from-solver refused (no artifacts dir for a target-only mode) -> submitted value directly\n{   \"stage\": \"done\",   \"name\": \"\\ud83c\\udf10 Back Up a Minute\",   \"lane\": \"web\",   \"worker\": null,   \"updated\": \"2026-10-19T21:49:53\",   \"launches\": 1,   \"help\": \"# Blocked: Target 1 never became available\\nThe GM returns only `{\\\"result\\\":\\\"preparing\\\", questions[...]}` for `hctf start` / `hctf status` (repeated several times). The body carries no target URL, host or artifact, and `hctf artifact` returns `invalid_delivery`. The contract names only \\\"Target 1\\\" (an old backup archive left exposed on a site). Without a target address I can't fetch the archive or recover the proof. Homebase is running (10.1.50.243).\\nNext step: re-run `hctf status web-exploitation-day-01-backup-exposure` until `result` changes from `preparing`, then look for the target base URL, fetch common backup paths named by the app itself (robots.txt / page links), and read the proof from the archive.\\n\",   \"attempt\": 1,   \"time_trial_result\": \"correct\",   \"mastery_result\": \"correct\" }\n{\"ts\": \"20261019T130527Z\", \"attempt\": null, \"answers\": {\"proof-1\": \"proof_7c36a256669a41b19d2547cce9463efd\"}, \"http\": 200, \"kind\": \"correct\", \"confirmed\": [\"proof-1\"], \"body\": {\"result\": \"CORRECT\", \"solved_by\": {\"name\": \"_blackb3ard\", \"at\": \"2026-10-19T13:05:25.991Z\"}, \"name\": \"🌐 Back Up a Minute\", \"flag\": \"d8415d70c76f50b5f5bfb0468cb53370\"}, \"transport\": \"homebase\", \"elapsed\": 2.28}\n\n######## day02/web-permission-to-slip\nYour neighbor's records are none of your business. Pity the object API never got that memo — see if you can slip into somebody else's row.\nproof-1 Target 1 Recover the proof from Target 1. trim\ntime_trial Your neighbor's records are none of your business. Pity the object API never got that memo — see if you can slip into somebody else's row. ['proof-1:Recover the proof from Target 1.']\nmastery Your neighbor's records are none of your business. Pity the object API never got that memo — see if you can slip into somebody else's row. ['proof-1:Recover the proof from Target 1.', 'proof-2:Recover the proof from Target 2.']\n# D2 web IDOR (Permission to Slip)\n- Live target: GM status returns `targets:[{id:\"Target 1\",url}]` after ~2 min of `result: preparing`; harness saves it as artifacts/c_targets.json (contract.json lacks it). Target returns 410 `{\"state\":\"completed\"}` once solved.\n- App: home \"Signed in as X\" + /briefs/<id> links; brief page fetch(\"/api/briefs/<id>\"); /api/history leaks a foreign case_id (owner executive, visibility reference_only); GET /api/briefs/<foreign> -> note `proof_<32hex>` (CORRECT).\n- solve.py: derives the API template from the brief page's fetch(), foreign ids from feed JSON, regex `proof[_-]...`; stdlib urllib + cookie jar.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- reference/techniques/web.md: live-target days -> targets come in status body `targets[]` (+ `routes[]`), not in contract.json; proof format `proof_<32 hex>`.\n{   \"stage\": \"done\",   \"name\": \"\\ud83c\\udf10 Permission to Slip\",   \"lane\": \"web\",   \"worker\": null,   \"updated\": \"2026-10-19T21:51:53\",   \"launches\": 1,   \"help\": \"# HELP: the single_solve regression case can't be replayed (the live target is gone)\\n\\n- The Single Solve is CORRECT (proof-1 = proof_3fecb9578e954b89ad02e72ba49e6287, confirmed.json).\\n- This is a live-target challenge. After the solve, the target host returns HTTP 410 `{\\\"state\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}` on every path.\\n  The case's contract.json is the early \\\"preparing\\\" body, which has no `targets`.\\n- The duel solve.py now resolves the target URL. It checks the contract `targets` first, then any *.json beside the\\n  contract or in the artifacts dir that carries `targets` (verified: it finds the URL in this case). Then it runs the\\n  IDOR chain: / -> /api/history -> foreign case ids -> the fetch() template from the case page (/api/briefs/<id>) -> regex\\n  `proof_...`.\\n- solver-test still reports got=null only because the backend is torn down. No offline bytes exist to replay, and\\n  hard-coding the confirmed value would break the \\\"derive from bytes\\\" rule.\\n- Harness ask: for web live-target lanes, skip the replay gate for single_solve once the GM confirms CORRECT, or record\\n  the target's HTTP responses during the solve so cases can replay them.\\n\",   \"attempt\": 1,   \"time_trial_result\": \"correct\",   \"mastery_result\": \"correct\" }\n{\"ts\": \"20261019T130419Z\", \"attempt\": null, \"answers\": {\"proof-1\": \"proof_3fecb9578e954b89ad02e72ba49e6287\"}, \"http\": 200, \"kind\": \"correct\", \"confirmed\": [\"proof-1\"], \"body\": {\"result\": \"CORRECT\", \"solved_by\": {\"name\": \"_blackb3ard\", \"at\": \"2026-10-19T13:04:18.000Z\"}, \"name\": \"🌐 Permission to Slip\", \"flag\": \"4329ceb5190a818e0ba9e200aa2dcc7d\"}, \"transport\": \"homebase\", \"elapsed\": 2.1}\n{\"ts\": \"2\n######## day03/web-query-me-this\nThe search box trusts you a little too much. Ask the database one pointed question and read the row it was never supposed to show you.\nproof-1 Target 1 Recover the proof from Target 1. trim\ntime_trial The search box trusts you a little too much. Ask the database one pointed question and read the row it was never supposed to show you. ['proof-1:Recover the proof from Target 1.']\nmastery The search box trusts you a little too much. Ask the database one pointed question and read the row it was never supposed to show you. ['proof-1:Recover the proof from Target 1.', 'proof-2:Recover the proof from Target 2.']\n- live target (contract.targets[].url), reachable directly (no hb exec). GET / -> form action=/lookup name=q (GET).\n- q=' / \"x' OR '1'='1\" / \"%' OR 1=1 --\" / UNION SELECT 1..5 -> \"Nothing matched\" (errors swallowed).\n- q=\"%' OR '1'='1\" -> 3 public rows only. WHERE wraps input in parentheses + a visibility AND.\n- q=\"zz') OR 1=1 --\" -> + hidden row pill 'restricted' \"Private escalation\" body proof_<32hex> => answer = proof_... token.\n- GM already CORRECT (parallel worker 13:03:28); target then returns HTTP 410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}.\n## Proposed lib additions\n- reference/techniques/web.md: D3 \"Query Me This\" = live target (contract.targets[{id:\"Target N\",url}]), search form GET /lookup?q=, SQLi needs paren close: `zz') OR 1=1 --`; proof is `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` in a hidden 'restricted' card. Target returns 410 {\"state\":\"completed\"} once the attempt is solved. Mastery set2 = Day 1 \"back up a minute\" (exposed backup archive) target.\n{   \"stage\": \"done\",   \"name\": \"\\ud83c\\udf10 Query Me This\",   \"lane\": \"web\",   \"worker\": null,   \"updated\": \"2026-10-19T21:54:10\",   \"launches\": 1,   \"help\": \"# web-query-me-this single_solve: solved, solver-test cannot replay\\n\\nThe Single Solve is CORRECT (GM 