{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDZH5RiQNbanPDwkAsx8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I rewrote `reference/techniques/web.md` and created `reference/coverage/web.md`. Nothing else was touched, and I ran no tests and no GM calls.\n\n- **Technique log:** The file still said \"web not released\", so I rewrote it to cover lane-days D01–D05. The GM ids number the lane's own days: D01–D03 came out on calendar day 19 and D04–D05 today. Both of today's challenges took under a minute to CORRECT: D04 was LFI (`reader.php?doc=../`×6 to `/run/huntress/objective.txt`) and D05 was an unprotected route named in `/api/clues`, whose JSON `evidence` field held the proof. It also records today's trouble: in D04 Mastery, Target 1 was a D01 backup site that the prompt didn't describe, and the solver stopped one link short of the `.json.bak`. The variant axes are filled in per concept (target mapping, Mastery mix and order, backup dir/file names, LFI params, clue routes, proof field names).\n- **Coverage atlas:** 31 concept rows (D01–D05 marked seen) and a 30-line cue block. There are 21 readiness gaps, 18 of them `prebuild`; the JSON is valid with the five required keys and no repeated ids. Priority 1: the depth-2 crawl and a dispatcher that runs every known concept on every target (today's failure), plus role tampering, JWT/session forgery, command injection, SSTI, SSRF and header/verb/path bypasses. I expect 2–3 new web bugs per calendar day.\n- **One gap won't drain on its own:** `hctf/prebuild.py` has no `web` lane, so tonight's prebuild can't build any of these gaps. I logged this as the `enable-web-prebuild-lane` note. Fixing it needs someone who owns `hctf/` to add the lane config and a minimal `lib/web.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":392,"cache_read_input_tokens":102993,"cache_creation":{"ephemer